(7046013, 1070267, 108580, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Alexkc:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by HarveyG:</b></div><hr/><i> Fingers in the triggers not a wise move, even if empty and "safe"... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Toy guns ;) </i></td></tr></table> Still no excuse! The bad habit persists when you do get a chance to fire or handle a real weapon. I''ve PM''d you the rest of my feelings :) Suffices to say one should not depict finger on trigger unless actually firing a weapon safely or in self defence...In terms of the art and mood you were depicting we can debate this one to the death. Oddly you got an HM. I say oddly because of the anti gun mood/voting I''ve seen reflect on DPC over the years. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Alexkc: Originally posted by HarveyG: Fingers in the triggers not a wise move, even if empty and "safe"...   Toy guns ;)  Still no excuse! The bad habit persists when you do get a chance to fire or handle a real weapon. I''ve PM''d you the rest of my feelings :) Suffices to say one should not depict finger on trigger unless actually firing a weapon safely or in self defence...In terms of the art and mood you were depicting we can debate this one to the death. Oddly you got an HM. I say oddly because of the anti gun mood/voting I''ve seen reflect on DPC over the years.  ', '2013-06-01 09:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
